    pr_ref:  # c2d6
    description: "WHAT\nRulings wanted on behaviour PR #2354 (stable-id v19) deliberately did not build, or built on a decision the coordinator or a package agent made without putting it to the owner. None of these is a tie two different declarations share (those are defect items: WI-zisam-sodaz-rosis-gutub-harug-gulih-lufat-gahus for C# #if, WI-zopan-fuviv-tuvam-foboz-rokof-jonod-kopus-julol for companions). Each point gives what was measured. Every \"build it\" answer moves stable ids and needs a scheme bump.\n\n1. Rust: a file's own top-level `#![cfg(...)]` is not read (inner #![cfg] of a mod/fn/impl/trait/extern body IS read since PR #2354). Cost of reading it: 9 more diesel ids move (2 test files). Benefit: it separates no tie (it applies to every item of the file alike). Guards agent's decision. Ruling: leave unread, or read for uniformity?\n\n2. C and Swift `||` / `&&` operands are not reordered: `#if defined(A) || defined(B)` and `#if defined(B) || defined(A)` give two ids; Swift `#if os(iOS) || os(macOS)` and reversed likewise (~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/v19_11232026/guards/repro_or_and/, output.txt: both APART). The owner's WI-sifar ruling B was \"sort the arguments and nothing more; do not try to evaluate the conditions\"; the coordinator applied it to Rust any()/all() argument lists only (diesel 173 and reqwest 6 ids moved by that sort) and did not put C/Swift operands to the owner (STATUS.md lines 28-29). Cost of sorting C/Swift operands: not measured. Ruling: does B cover `||`/`&&` operands?\n\n3. TypeScript outer parameters: `f(x?: number)` and `f(x: number)` hash alike (both hgstableid18:9a3af27e3d5ad247 on base and after; ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/v19_11232026/jsts/fixtures_jsts.txt lines 6-9, fixture jsts/c_dozos.ts), and `...xs: T[]` / `xs: T[]` hash alike; but `f(x: number = 5)` hashes apart from `f(x: number)` (has-a-default is hashed, WI-dozos rule 1), and since PR #2354 interface MEMBERS hash `?T` and `...T`. The owner ruled WI-dozos \"as you would pick\"; the coordinator's pick, as written in the build brief, reads \"the parameter's type and optionality stay\": the code does not hash `?` for an outer parameter, so that sentence was wrong about `?` (it is true of having a default). Ruling: hash `?` and `...` for outer parameters (moves every TS callable with an optional or rest parameter; not counted), or leave as is?\n\n4. Vue/Svelte component script variables, interfaces, type aliases and enums were NOT re-anchored on the component's file: their backstop table formula hashes the member's own language + path + name, with no file anchor (components agent). The WI-vavag ruling read \"every member declared in the file follows the corrected file stable id\"; functions, methods and fields did (koel 1,283, workadventure 1,660 ids moved). Not moved: koel ts variable 633, interface 5, type 4; workadventure ts variable 2,162, js variable 6, enum/interface/type 16. Ruling: re-anchor these too (about 642 + 2,184 more ids on those two trees), or accept that the table formula has no file anchor?\n\n5. Julia `Base.X` / `Core.X` are not folded to bare `X`: folding needs Base's export list, and an unexported `Base.X` is not the bare `X` (types agent). No Julia repository on this machine; fixture only. Ruling: ship an export list, or leave apart?\n\n6. Julia relative paths `.Sub.X` and `Sub.X` are kept apart (types agent: deliberate, conservative, like Python's). Ruling: confirm.\n\n7. Solidity `address payable` and `address` are kept apart (types agent, 1e5bbbfea: the sized-alias fold covers uint/int/ufixed/fixed/byte only). Ruling: confirm.\n\n8. Prisma `model` stays kind `class` (not in the WI-lilab ruling's list; kinds agent). PR #2354 already moved all 161 / 161 model ids on 13 real schemas (hashed word model -> class); a later kind change moves them again. Ruling: keep `class`, or pick a kind now and move once more?\n\n9. layout_free spaces JS expressions by its own rule, not JS's (`tab == = 'a'`): the hashed text only, nothing displayed (locals agent). koel: 291 / 2,353 Vue directive ids moved in PR #2354 by the layout-free bound expression. Ruling: accept a hash-only spacing, or write a JS-aware one (moves directive ids again)?\n\n10. Doc and table formulas (WI-radim's open question, which PR #2354 did not answer; STATUS.md line 30): is a doc symbol's NAME meant to be layout-free at all (a Markdown heading is content)? The Svelte block's own name still keeps its layout (locals agent); Swift #if scope labels sit in table names, so a universal table-formula rule needs its own replay. PR #2354 built only the Elixir module (plausible: 0 of 1,189 modules moved) and the Vue/Svelte bound expression. WI-radim is closed by PR #2354; the question lives here. WI-radim's own \"also not checked\" lines (a \"//\" comment that ends a hashed text with no line break after it; \"|\" before \"{\" unspaced in the canonical spelling) were not checked in PR #2354 either.\n\n11. Ratify three decisions the coordinator made without the owner (STATUS.md lines 28-31, 157-160):\n    a. WI-juzom \"decide whether to canonicalize\": YES was built (C#: lwip 17 / 1,007 and sherpa-onnx dotnet 177 / 900 ids moved; Swift: vapor 3, swift-nio 3).\n    b. WI-vavag: component members keep language typescript/javascript; only the file stable id they hash changed.\n    c. WI-finam extended to JavaScript/TypeScript (one commit, 4a0b62b8f in the package, 0fc3c7f6e on the PR branch): moved knex 727 / 11,346, hocuspocus 150 / 2,721, nest/packages 698 / 11,930 ids, for named-local pre-split tie groups knex 39 -> 34, hocuspocus 85 -> 85, nest 103 -> 103. It is one commit and can be reverted alone (that moves those ids back and needs a bump).\n    d. Fixes extended past the languages their items named, under the standing rule that a filed item asks for a general fix: built-in type spellings to Go, Solidity and Rust (compose-go 61 / 1,727, zksync-era contracts 43 / 965, diesel 6 ids moved); preprocessor branches to CUDA, HLSL, GLSL and Objective-C (whisper.cpp ggml-cuda 98 / 965, Vulkan shaders 160 / 498, AFNetworking 255 / 1,051, CocoaLumberjack 97 / 2,030); locals to Scala, Dart, PHP, C++ and HLSL (sbt main 450 / 5,140, libzmq 4, bullet HLSL 6); a V function with a receiver is kind method (fixture only); a TypeScript type predicate names its subject by position (#0 is T).\n\n12. WI-hodin point 6 (closed by ruling: message_dispatch stand-ins in a .svelte file stay \"javascript\") rested on parity with \"the functions and the file node of a .svelte script\". PR #2354 moved that file node to the `svelte:` slot (WI-vavag); the functions stay javascript/typescript. Parity with the file node no longer holds; parity with the functions does. Not measured. Ruling: keep, or revisit.\n\n13. WI-dozos's side question was not ruled and WI-dozos is closed on its three rules: does raising a PyPI grammar constraint in pyproject.toml bump SHAPE_ID_SCHEME? vendor-sync.md says bump for a vendored re-sync and nothing for a PyPI constraint raise; docs/audits/0009 line 47 says the decision \"belongs in an ADR-0014 amendment\", and ADR-0014 is retired.\n\nREPRO\nPer point above (fixture paths given where one exists).\n\nMEASURED\nAs stated per point; every figure is the named package agent's or the coordinator's, on the tree named.\n\nNOT CHECKED\nPoint 2 and point 3 cost (number of ids that would move): not counted on any tree. Point 12: not measured.\n\nFound 2026-11-23/24 while building PR #2354 (stable-id v19). Detail: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/v19_11232026/STATUS.md (lines 28-31, 43, 57, 75-76, 94, 118, 147-148, 157-160), ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/v19_11232026/{guards,types,jsts,components,kinds,locals}/RESULTS.md"  # c2d6
    fields: {}  # c2d6
