  message: "OWNER RULING 2026-11-24 (in session): \"v20 with pohom, hodin 4/7 and siror 3, rest as recommended\". The recommendations as put to the owner, by point:\n1. Rust file-level #![cfg]: LEAVE UNREAD (separates no tie).\n2. C/Swift || and && operands: LEAVE, not reordered (no tie; needs expression parsing, not a sort).\n3. TypeScript outer parameters: HASH ? and ... in the v20 bump. Proxy cost put to the owner: 1,834 of 43,495 TS callables (4.2%) in the 49 stored v19 maps show ? or ... in their displayed signature.\n4. Vue/Svelte component variables, interfaces, type aliases, enums: ACCEPT, not re-anchored (the table formula anchors them by path).\n5. Julia Base.X / Core.X: LEAVE APART. 6. Julia .Sub.X / Sub.X: KEPT APART, confirmed.\n7. Solidity address payable / address: KEPT APART, confirmed.\n8. Prisma model: KEEP kind class.\n9. layout_free spacing of JS expressions: ACCEPT (hash input only).\n10. Doc and table names: LEAVE (a heading is content); not urgent. WI-radim's \"also not checked\" lines stay unchecked.\n11. a, b, c, d: ALL RATIFIED (11c put to the owner as poor value, about 1,575 ids for 5 tie groups, harmless before a release).\n12. message_dispatch stand-ins in a .svelte file: KEEP javascript (parity with the functions holds).\n13. A PyPI grammar constraint raise: the same test as a vendored re-sync, bump SHAPE_ID_SCHEME only if shape ids changed. Put to the owner with the caveat that only a few lines of docs/grammars/vendor-sync.md were read for it.\nStatus moves to todo_soft: point 3 is to build in v20; every other point is closed by the ruling."  # 429e
